* 1998–2003 [[Honda Inspire]]
* 1999 [[Honda Saber]]

==J30==
The J30A displaces {{cvt|2997|cc|L cc cuin|1|order=out}} and is a [[SOHC]] [[VTEC]] design. Its bore and stroke is {{cvt|86x86|mm|in|2}}. Output for the J30A1 was initially {{cvt|200|hp|kW|0}} and {{cvt|195|lbft|Nm|0}} of torque, later increased to {{cvt|210|hp|kW|0}} and {{cvt|200|lbft|Nm|0}} of torque. The J30A4 pushed output to {{cvt|242|hp|kW|0}} and {{cvt|212|lbft|Nm|0}} using a three-way VTEC system, a higher (10.0:1) [[compression ratio]] and a novel [[exhaust manifold]] cast as one piece with the cylinder head. It weighs nearly {{cvt|20|lb}} less and is an inch shorter than J30A1. This version was on the [[Ward's 10 Best Engines]] list for 2003 and 2004. The [[Integrated Motor Assist|IMA]] [[hybrid car|hybrid]] version was on the list for 2005. In 2006 Honda created the J30A5 to mark the 30th anniversary of the Accord. It boosted output to {{cvt|244|hp|kW|0}} ([[Horsepower#SAE net power|SAE Net]] 08/04) and {{cvt|211|lbft|Nm|0}} (SAE Net 08/04) of torque. According to Honda, horsepower gains were achieved with improvements to the airflow of the intake and exhaust system.
