==J32==
The '''J32A''' displaces {{cvt|3210|cc|L cc cuin|1|order=out}} and is a [[SOHC]] [[VTEC]] design. Its bore and stroke is {{cvt|89x86|mm|in|2}}. Output was {{cvt|225|hp|kW|0}} at 5600&nbsp;rpm and {{cvt|217|lbft|Nm|0}} at 4700&nbsp;rpm for the J32A1, with the J32A2 raising output to {{cvt|260|hp|kW|0}} at 6200&nbsp;rpm and {{cvt|232|lbft|Nm|0}} at 3500–5500&nbsp;rpm. A more aggressive camshaft, more free flowing intake/exhaust, and a 2-stage intake manifold produced a {{cvt|33.55|hp|kW}} increase over the J32A1. The J32A3's output in the 2004/2005 TL is {{cvt|270|hp|kW|0}}. Due to changes in SAE testing methods, 2006–2008 model years have a reduced output rating of {{cvt|258|hp|kW|0}}, despite being mechanically identical. The J32A3 includes a one-piece exhaust manifold cast with the cylinder head, first introduced on the J30A4.

